1
00:00:00,667 --> 00:00:04,833
<i> [BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

2
00:00:07,233 --> 00:00:08,333
<i>- Hey!
- Hey!</i>

3
00:00:08,467 --> 00:00:10,600
<i> Hey! Hey! My bag!</i>

4
00:00:10,733 --> 00:00:13,200
<i>Previously on
You're My Favorite Song...</i>

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:15,133
<i> You're crazy, Calix!</i>

6
00:00:16,367 --> 00:00:19,167
<i>There! Someone took my bag,
Zion.</i>

7
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:20,733
<i> [OBJECTS CLATTER]</i>

8
00:00:20,867 --> 00:00:21,700
<i> - Wait! Wait!
-</i> Where are you going?

9
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:22,667
<i>- Just wait!
- Where are you go...</i>

10
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:24,133
<i>Why did you destroy our resort?</i>

11
00:00:24,267 --> 00:00:25,800
<i> Yes.</i>

12
00:00:25,933 --> 00:00:26,867
<i> [XAVI THUDS]</i>

13
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:27,600
<i> Dad!</i>

14
00:00:27,767 --> 00:00:30,167
<i> [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

15
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:31,733
<i> Dad, Dad!</i>

16
00:00:31,867 --> 00:00:33,167
<i> My child.</i>

17
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:34,333
<i> Dad.</i>

18
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:38,367
<i>My grandfather Xavi
is in the hospital, Zion.</i>

19
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:42,567
<i> [ZION GRUNTS]</i>

20
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:44,100
<i>- Angel, run now, hurry!
- Hey! Let go of me! Hey!</i>

21
00:00:44,233 --> 00:00:46,100
<i>- Angel, run.
- Move aside!</i>

22
00:00:46,233 --> 00:00:48,033
- Let go of me!
- Angel, hurry!

23
00:00:48,167 --> 00:00:50,867
<i>The person who bought that
is someone dear to you.</i>

24
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:51,933
<i> Who?</i>

25
00:00:52,067 --> 00:00:53,633
<i> Your wife.</i>

26
00:00:53,967 --> 00:00:55,167
<i> Happy anniversary.</i>

27
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:56,867
<i>Are you having an affair
with Tyrone?</i>

28
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,133
<i>Is that really how low
you think of me?</i>

29
00:01:00,267 --> 00:01:03,533
<i>You think I'm having an
affair with my driver?</i>

30
00:01:03,667 --> 00:01:10,800
<i>♪ 'Cause baby,
you are my favorite song ♪</i>

31
00:01:10,967 --> 00:01:14,233
<i>♪ I'll put you on repeat
all night ♪</i>

32
00:01:14,367 --> 00:01:18,233
<i> ♪ I know I'll never move on ♪</i>

33
00:01:18,367 --> 00:01:21,767
<i>♪ My first,
right where I belong ♪</i>

34
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:29,000
<i>♪ You are my first
heartbeat song ♪</i>

35
00:01:37,867 --> 00:01:38,733
Gino.

36
00:01:38,867 --> 00:01:40,400
Sir, do we have somewhere to go?

37
00:01:40,567 --> 00:01:41,967
- I'll get the car.
- No, no, Gino.

38
00:01:45,833 --> 00:01:47,133
You're loyal to me, right?

39
00:01:48,533 --> 00:01:49,533
Of course, Sir.

40
00:01:49,667 --> 00:01:51,033
I've been with you
for a long time.

41
00:01:53,233 --> 00:01:54,967
I want you to follow my wife.

42
00:01:56,033 --> 00:01:58,333
Watch her movements closely.

43
00:01:58,467 --> 00:02:00,833
See if she's doing anything
behind my back.

44
00:02:05,767 --> 00:02:07,633
Okay, Sir.

45
00:02:07,767 --> 00:02:08,667
All right.

46
00:02:25,733 --> 00:02:29,767
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

47
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,400
[XAVI COUGHING]

48
00:02:31,533 --> 00:02:32,433
Grandfather.

49
00:02:32,567 --> 00:02:34,100
Grandfather.

50
00:02:34,233 --> 00:02:36,567
Grandfather Xavi, how are you?

51
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:38,500
Are you having trouble
breathing?

52
00:02:40,467 --> 00:02:41,333
[CLICKS TONGUE]

53
00:02:41,467 --> 00:02:43,200
Don't worry, my dear,

54
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:46,567
your grandfather
is still strong.

55
00:02:51,033 --> 00:02:52,200
You know,

56
00:02:53,267 --> 00:02:55,033
the only thing
I'm worried about is

57
00:02:57,467 --> 00:02:58,967
who those

58
00:03:00,033 --> 00:03:04,433
thugs were who destroyed
our resort.

59
00:03:04,567 --> 00:03:05,500
Do you know that

60
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:08,300
because of them,

61
00:03:08,433 --> 00:03:11,967
our grand opening was ruined.

62
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:13,267
Dad.

63
00:03:14,767 --> 00:03:17,200
Stop thinking about the resort
for now.

64
00:03:17,333 --> 00:03:19,833
What matters now is that
you get better.

65
00:03:19,967 --> 00:03:22,633
I'll handle everything.

66
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:27,233
I'll double my live selling of
turon so we can get more orders.

67
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,867
Mom Bebe, I'll help.

68
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,567
I'll find a way to earn money.

69
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:37,100
Oh, child, no need.

70
00:03:37,233 --> 00:03:38,433
Don't worry about it.

71
00:03:38,567 --> 00:03:40,100
Mom Bebe can handle it.

72
00:03:40,233 --> 00:03:41,367
I'll take care of everything.

73
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:44,467
What matters is you focus on
your studies.

74
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:46,233
I'll handle everything,

75
00:03:46,367 --> 00:03:48,100
okay?

76
00:03:48,233 --> 00:03:50,200
There you go.

77
00:03:50,333 --> 00:03:52,233
See? That's what
I've been saying.

78
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:55,833
You're just getting stressed.

79
00:03:57,967 --> 00:03:59,667
We might as well

80
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,433
just go home.

81
00:04:02,467 --> 00:04:04,667
Didn't the doctor say

82
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:07,233
I still have a year left?

83
00:04:07,367 --> 00:04:08,500
Then let's go home

84
00:04:08,633 --> 00:04:11,133
- and stop wasting money.
- Grandfather,

85
00:04:11,267 --> 00:04:13,300
- what are you saying?
- [BEBE SIGHS HEAVILY]

86
00:04:13,433 --> 00:04:15,767
You always talk like that.

87
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:21,900
It's like you're so eager
to leave us.

88
00:04:24,667 --> 00:04:26,767
Don't you want to be with us?

89
00:04:32,933 --> 00:04:35,500
It's not like that, my dear.

90
00:04:35,633 --> 00:04:37,700
You know me,

91
00:04:37,833 --> 00:04:39,600
I just don't want

92
00:04:39,733 --> 00:04:42,133
to be a burden to you.

93
00:04:44,367 --> 00:04:47,567
Grandfather Xavi,
you're not a burden to us.

94
00:04:48,733 --> 00:04:52,433
You will never be a burden
to those who love you.

95
00:04:53,867 --> 00:04:56,833
That's why we're fixing
the resort, right?

96
00:04:56,967 --> 00:04:59,100
You even made me a promise.

97
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:03,967
You said you'd undergo
chemotherapy

98
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:07,033
once Gran Vista starts
earning well.

99
00:05:13,667 --> 00:05:17,267
I know you want to see
grandmother in heaven,

100
00:05:18,300 --> 00:05:20,867
but Mom Bebe and I
are still here.

101
00:05:21,933 --> 00:05:24,433
Stay here with us for now, okay?

102
00:05:39,033 --> 00:05:40,467
I'm sorry, my dear.

103
00:05:44,333 --> 00:05:46,167
Sometimes I forget

104
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:49,633
how much you love me.

105
00:05:51,567 --> 00:05:52,667
You're right,

106
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:56,167
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

107
00:05:56,300 --> 00:05:58,133
I need to get stronger first.

108
00:06:00,367 --> 00:06:03,033
Then we'll grow Gran Vista

109
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,000
and...

110
00:06:07,133 --> 00:06:08,800
I'll get treatment.

111
00:06:15,533 --> 00:06:16,800
I'm sorry.

112
00:06:20,367 --> 00:06:21,767
I'm sorry, my dear.

113
00:06:31,167 --> 00:06:32,333
Group hug.

114
00:06:32,467 --> 00:06:35,667
["YOU'RE MY FAVORITE SONG"
INSTRUMENTAL]

115
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,333
I'm sorry, my child.

116
00:06:47,433 --> 00:06:53,967
♪ Feelings inside my chest ♪

117
00:06:56,533 --> 00:06:59,200
♪ Rising up ♪

118
00:06:59,333 --> 00:07:03,800
♪ to my throat ♪

119
00:07:04,967 --> 00:07:08,133
♪ If I say it out loud ♪

120
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:12,733
♪ Will you listen? ♪

121
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:21,133
♪ Or should I just keep
my mouth shut? ♪

122
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:46,000
Angel?

123
00:07:50,733 --> 00:07:52,433
I'm not Angel.

124
00:07:53,567 --> 00:07:54,867
I'm sorry.

125
00:08:11,533 --> 00:08:12,500
Thank you.

126
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:17,367
Zion.

127
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:20,833
Thank you for helping
me escape yesterday.

128
00:08:25,167 --> 00:08:27,867
But Grandfather Xavi,
needs surgery.

129
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:34,367
Wait did Calix beat you up?

130
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:39,167
I fought back a bit?

131
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,400
I mean,

132
00:08:41,533 --> 00:08:44,100
I did land a punch on Poncy,
but it didn't matter,

133
00:08:44,233 --> 00:08:46,467
there were too many of them,
they ganged up on me.

134
00:08:47,567 --> 00:08:49,067
Come on, let's go to the clinic.

135
00:08:50,167 --> 00:08:52,400
Angel, it's fine.

136
00:08:52,533 --> 00:08:54,533
It might just
make things worse.

137
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:57,200
I'll just tell Ma'am Dragona...

138
00:08:57,333 --> 00:09:00,233
I don't know, that I fell down
the stairs?

139
00:09:00,367 --> 00:09:01,233
That I hit my head?

140
00:09:01,367 --> 00:09:02,233
Right?

141
00:09:03,267 --> 00:09:04,500
Are you sure?

142
00:09:04,633 --> 00:09:06,233
Yeah, I'm fine.

143
00:09:06,367 --> 00:09:07,767
Did I hear my name?

144
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:09,700
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

145
00:09:09,833 --> 00:09:11,167
Ma'am Dragona, no.

146
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:13,000
We weren't talking about you.

147
00:09:14,833 --> 00:09:15,700
Angel,

148
00:09:15,833 --> 00:09:16,767
come to my office.

149
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:18,633
I need to talk to you and Calix.

150
00:09:18,767 --> 00:09:20,033
Yes, Ma'am.

151
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:22,833
Oh no!

152
00:09:22,967 --> 00:09:24,767
Could this be because
of what happened yesterday?

153
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:29,000
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

154
00:09:34,367 --> 00:09:36,100
Calix and I might get expelled.

155
00:09:38,900 --> 00:09:39,967
Oh no.

156
00:09:41,567 --> 00:09:42,633
Now, Angel.

157
00:09:46,033 --> 00:09:47,867
Wait. Yes, Ma'am.

158
00:09:50,833 --> 00:09:55,567
[SOFT TENSE MUSIC]

159
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:56,633
Ma'am Dragona...

160
00:09:56,867 --> 00:09:57,933
what happened yesterday,

161
00:09:58,067 --> 00:09:59,900
Calix was the one
who started it.

162
00:10:00,033 --> 00:10:01,267
I'll explain everything.

163
00:10:03,967 --> 00:10:05,233
What happened yesterday?

164
00:10:07,867 --> 00:10:08,867
Do it, Calix.

165
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,400
Punch her.

166
00:10:10,533 --> 00:10:11,567
- Hey!
- Hey!

167
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:12,600
Hey!

168
00:10:12,733 --> 00:10:14,200
- My bag!
- For three!

169
00:10:17,133 --> 00:10:18,433
- Angel, run now, hurry!
- Hey! Let go of me!

170
00:10:18,567 --> 00:10:20,967
- Hey! Angel, run!
- Move aside!

171
00:10:29,333 --> 00:10:31,500
Ah, Ma'am Dragona...

172
00:10:31,633 --> 00:10:33,500
why did you call us here?

173
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:34,767
I was just about to review

174
00:10:34,933 --> 00:10:37,033
for the Regional Quizcon
tomorrow.

175
00:10:37,167 --> 00:10:39,300
That's exactly why you're here.

176
00:10:39,433 --> 00:10:41,800
Calix, your partner, Frida,

177
00:10:41,933 --> 00:10:43,733
cannot join you
at the Quizcon tomorrow

178
00:10:43,867 --> 00:10:46,200
because she's in the hospital.

179
00:10:46,333 --> 00:10:49,033
And that's the reason
why you are here, Angel.

180
00:10:50,733 --> 00:10:54,300
I want you to be Calix's
new partner

181
00:10:54,433 --> 00:10:56,733
for the Regional Quizcon...

182
00:10:57,833 --> 00:11:00,767
which will be happening
tomorrow.

183
00:11:00,900 --> 00:11:02,600
Regional Quizcon, Ma'am?

184
00:11:02,733 --> 00:11:04,233
And it's already tomorrow?

185
00:11:04,367 --> 00:11:05,433
Yes.

186
00:11:05,567 --> 00:11:08,233
I know it's crunch time
for review...

187
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:13,400
but because of your outstanding
performance in this school,

188
00:11:13,533 --> 00:11:14,800
I have enough faith in you.

189
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:27,067
Don't you dare accept this.

190
00:11:30,967 --> 00:11:33,300
If you do,
I'll make your life hell.

191
00:11:34,333 --> 00:11:35,767
I don't want you as my partner.

192
00:11:49,433 --> 00:11:50,867
Okay.

193
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:56,600
Well, the prize money will be
35,000 pesos.

194
00:11:56,733 --> 00:12:01,300
And if you win, you'll split it
between the two of you.

195
00:12:03,967 --> 00:12:06,633
I'll handle everything.

196
00:12:06,767 --> 00:12:10,767
I'll double my live selling
of turon so we get more orders.

197
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:16,933
Mama Bebe, I'll help.

198
00:12:17,067 --> 00:12:19,400
I'll find a way to earn money.

199
00:12:22,133 --> 00:12:24,567
I accept, Ma'am Dragona.

200
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:34,367
[STIRRING MUSIC]

201
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:35,667
Very good.

202
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:40,267
Last year, Brighton Bay Academy
won the Regional Quizcon.

203
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:43,167
And according to the organizers,

204
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:45,600
the games this year will be
different

205
00:12:45,733 --> 00:12:47,567
and much more difficult.

206
00:12:50,300 --> 00:12:51,200
Okay?

207
00:12:51,333 --> 00:12:55,167
So I'll leave the two of you
to review, okay?

208
00:12:59,833 --> 00:13:02,567
And you're both excused
from all your classes today.

209
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:05,000
Okay? So you can focus
on reviewing.

210
00:13:05,133 --> 00:13:06,933
- All right.
- Yes. Thank you, Ma'am.

211
00:13:07,067 --> 00:13:08,933
Okay.

212
00:13:09,067 --> 00:13:11,000
Thank you so much,
Ma'am Dragona.

213
00:13:13,567 --> 00:13:20,000
[TENSE MUSIC]

214
00:13:20,133 --> 00:13:22,733
You heard Ma'am Dragona,
let's start reviewing.

215
00:13:25,733 --> 00:13:26,600
Fine.

216
00:13:26,733 --> 00:13:28,433
I'll ask first.

217
00:13:28,567 --> 00:13:30,333
Question number one...

218
00:13:30,467 --> 00:13:34,567
why do you have the nerve
to agree to be my partner?

219
00:13:37,533 --> 00:13:39,533
If you hadn't come
to Brighton Bay Academy,

220
00:13:39,667 --> 00:13:42,000
someone else would've been
assigned to me.

221
00:13:42,133 --> 00:13:46,200
So why don't you just quit?

222
00:13:46,333 --> 00:13:47,267
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

223
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:49,500
I don't want you as a partner
either, Calix.

224
00:13:49,633 --> 00:13:52,767
Do you think I want someone like
you-self-centered,

225
00:13:52,900 --> 00:13:55,267
narcissistic, annoying,
and entitled-as a partner?

226
00:14:01,100 --> 00:14:03,067
But I need this...

227
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:04,600
so even if your attitude
is terrible,

228
00:14:04,733 --> 00:14:06,100
I'll put up with you, Calix.

229
00:14:08,567 --> 00:14:10,100
You talk too much.

230
00:14:13,533 --> 00:14:16,100
Stay out of my way
at the Quizcon tomorrow.

231
00:14:19,367 --> 00:14:21,867
I can win the Quizcon
even on my own.

232
00:14:31,300 --> 00:14:32,533
You're so arrogant.

233
00:14:38,967 --> 00:14:40,467
You can do this, Angel.

234
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:42,033
[BRIGHT MUSIC]

235
00:14:42,167 --> 00:14:43,800
Do this for Grandfather Xavi.

236
00:14:51,467 --> 00:14:53,067
Oh no, my bag.

237
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:54,933
You're crazy, Calix!

238
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:11,900
Calix is really insane,
he hung my bag up here.

239
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:27,933
[ANGEL GRUNTING]

240
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:09,433
If it's okay with you,

241
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:11,333
I can lift you up.

242
00:16:11,467 --> 00:16:15,300
["UNANG PAG-IBIG" BY
HEATH, CLIFFORD, AND MARCO]

243
00:16:15,433 --> 00:16:16,800
You seem familiar.

244
00:16:37,633 --> 00:16:38,833
Yup, it's me, Angel.

245
00:16:38,967 --> 00:16:41,900
- ♪ How have you been? ♪
- [MIGUEL CHUCKLES]

246
00:16:42,067 --> 00:16:45,567
♪ Are you still there? ♪

247
00:16:45,700 --> 00:16:52,800
♪ It's been so long
since we last met ♪

248
00:16:52,933 --> 00:16:56,967
♪ Do you still remember the... ♪

249
00:16:58,433 --> 00:17:00,967
What are you doing here in
Solmera City?

250
00:17:01,100 --> 00:17:03,467
My family and I live here now.

251
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:05,100
Really?

252
00:17:05,233 --> 00:17:06,433
You might just be making
that up

253
00:17:06,567 --> 00:17:07,767
maybe you're actually a stalker.

254
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:09,900
Hey, no way.

255
00:17:10,033 --> 00:17:12,300
This is my father's hometown.

256
00:17:12,433 --> 00:17:14,600
[LAUGHS]
Just kidding.

257
00:17:14,767 --> 00:17:17,400
I thought we'd never see each
other again.

258
00:17:17,533 --> 00:17:19,400
I thought so too.

259
00:17:19,533 --> 00:17:20,833
Did you miss me?

260
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:25,933
- ♪ Walking home together ♪
- As a friend.

261
00:17:26,067 --> 00:17:28,633
- ♪ Not in a hurry ♪
- [ANGEL CHUCKLES]

262
00:17:28,767 --> 00:17:31,067
Of course, as a friend,
I missed you.

263
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:34,000
I also missed listening
to your songs.

264
00:17:34,133 --> 00:17:36,700
Have you written a lot
of new songs again?

265
00:17:36,833 --> 00:17:38,967
Yeah, I'll play some for you.

266
00:17:39,100 --> 00:17:40,567
But

267
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:42,200
let's get your bag first.

268
00:17:43,567 --> 00:17:48,833
- ♪In case it comes back to me♪
- Let's get it.

269
00:17:50,433 --> 00:17:52,600
- ♪ The first... ♪
- I got you.

270
00:17:52,733 --> 00:17:53,800
Don't worry, Angel.

271
00:17:53,933 --> 00:17:55,867
[LAUGHS]
Let's get it.

272
00:17:58,933 --> 00:18:01,900
- Wait, there, there over there.
- ♪ of fading away ♪

273
00:18:02,033 --> 00:18:06,067
- ♪ The first love... ♪
- Can you carry me too?

274
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:07,200
Wait, me.

275
00:18:09,133 --> 00:18:11,900
- Your head is just too big.
- ♪ I'll just whisper it ♪

276
00:18:12,033 --> 00:18:14,100
♪ To the wind ♪

277
00:18:17,167 --> 00:18:27,133
[GUITAR STRUMMING]

278
00:18:41,967 --> 00:18:43,067
That's beautiful.

279
00:18:45,167 --> 00:18:46,467
Thank you.

280
00:18:46,600 --> 00:18:48,533
It's my new song...

281
00:18:48,667 --> 00:18:50,100
but it's still not quite
there yet.

282
00:18:50,233 --> 00:18:52,633
I'm still figuring it out.

283
00:18:52,767 --> 00:18:55,933
You know,
I think you'll make it big.

284
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:57,667
Like Miguel from Siklab.

285
00:18:59,933 --> 00:19:01,033
Are you a fan of Siklab?

286
00:19:02,633 --> 00:19:03,600
Just a bit.

287
00:19:03,733 --> 00:19:05,967
My classmates are bigger fans.

288
00:19:06,100 --> 00:19:08,733
Their songs are good too but...

289
00:19:08,867 --> 00:19:10,867
I like your original songs more.

290
00:19:13,733 --> 00:19:16,000
My dad is...

291
00:19:16,133 --> 00:19:17,400
he's very controlling.

292
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,933
He takes creative control
of my work.

293
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:23,400
Sorry, what was that?

294
00:19:25,767 --> 00:19:26,900
Nothing, it's nothing.

295
00:19:27,033 --> 00:19:28,333
It's nothing.

296
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:33,100
I just said thank you
for appreciating my songs.

297
00:19:34,867 --> 00:19:37,333
Oh, here.

298
00:19:37,467 --> 00:19:40,900
Sorry, my budget's a bit tight,
so this is all I could get.

299
00:19:41,033 --> 00:19:42,633
It's a thank-you for your help.

300
00:19:44,167 --> 00:19:45,600
Thank you.

301
00:19:45,733 --> 00:19:47,600
This is my favorite.

302
00:19:47,733 --> 00:19:49,333
But I can't eat this right now.

303
00:19:49,467 --> 00:19:51,533
You know I can't show you
my face.

304
00:19:54,533 --> 00:19:56,533
You're really something?

305
00:19:56,667 --> 00:19:58,067
All right then.
I'll go along with your thing,

306
00:19:58,200 --> 00:20:00,667
Captain Serenade,
just so you'll eat that.

307
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:03,500
I won't look while you eat,
promise.

308
00:20:03,667 --> 00:20:04,967
Promise?

309
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:06,033
No peeking.

310
00:20:07,067 --> 00:20:08,467
Yes, here I go.

311
00:20:10,433 --> 00:20:20,400
["UNANG PAG-IBIG" BY
HEATH, CLIFFORD, AND MARCO]

312
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,967
How have you been?

313
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:44,500
Are you still there?

314
00:20:44,633 --> 00:20:51,967
It's been so long
since we last met...

315
00:20:52,100 --> 00:20:54,700
- Do you still remember?
- Thank you.

316
00:20:54,833 --> 00:20:58,600
And good luck
with your Quizcon tomorrow,

317
00:20:58,733 --> 00:20:59,700
the one you mentioned.

318
00:21:01,533 --> 00:21:03,533
Thank you.

319
00:21:03,667 --> 00:21:05,800
I hope we win even though...

320
00:21:05,933 --> 00:21:08,467
Calix is like an unpredictable
variable in an equation.

321
00:21:08,633 --> 00:21:09,667
You don't know if he'll help

322
00:21:09,800 --> 00:21:14,000
- or just cause trouble.
- Always side by side...

323
00:21:14,133 --> 00:21:16,267
I'm sure you'll win.

324
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:18,767
You're smart.

325
00:21:18,900 --> 00:21:20,100
And I believe in you.

326
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:24,600
Sorry you can't eat.

327
00:21:24,733 --> 00:21:25,900
Want me to feed you?

328
00:21:27,533 --> 00:21:30,600
Okay, I'm kind of hungry too.

329
00:21:30,733 --> 00:21:31,533
Open your mouth.

330
00:21:38,367 --> 00:21:39,500
Thank you.

331
00:21:42,867 --> 00:21:49,467
In case it comes back to me...

332
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:52,933
<i> You're only seventeen,</i>

333
00:21:53,067 --> 00:21:54,533
<i>it's like you threw your life
away.</i>

334
00:21:54,667 --> 00:21:56,867
<i>Fine, fine!
If I threw it away, then I did!</i>

335
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:59,167
<i> You should have been the one
'</i> who died...

336
00:21:59,300 --> 00:22:01,400
<i> instead of Mom who loved me.</i>

337
00:22:09,833 --> 00:22:10,967
Hey.

338
00:22:11,100 --> 00:22:12,933
Hey, what are you doing?

339
00:22:13,067 --> 00:22:15,400
Someone might see us here.

340
00:22:15,567 --> 00:22:16,500
Don't overthink it.

341
00:22:18,133 --> 00:22:19,100
I know you missed this too.

342
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:32,033
I feel like I recognize
that boy over there.

343
00:22:32,167 --> 00:22:35,000
I think he's one of the ones
who destroyed our resort.

344
00:22:35,133 --> 00:22:36,700
I think I know them.

345
00:22:36,833 --> 00:22:39,233
Kaila, do you know where I can
find them?

346
00:22:39,367 --> 00:22:41,267
I need to know their reason

347
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:43,467
why they destroyed our resort

348
00:22:43,600 --> 00:22:45,700
or if someone ordered them
to do it.

349
00:22:45,833 --> 00:22:47,167
[PEOPLE CHEERING]

350
00:22:47,300 --> 00:22:50,000
If you're really nervous,
you can just stay quiet.

351
00:22:50,167 --> 00:22:53,100
"Which branch of mathematics
is considered...

352
00:22:53,233 --> 00:22:55,733
the 'queen of mathematics'?"

353
00:22:55,867 --> 00:22:58,033
I'm not sure but...

354
00:22:58,167 --> 00:23:00,333
I think it's number theory?

355
00:23:00,467 --> 00:23:01,500
I think it's number theory too.

356
00:23:01,633 --> 00:23:11,600
["YOU'RE MY FAVORITE SONG"
BY PRINCESS ALIYAH]
